From 14025b67a990f747a4fbbf80a99ebdef3835efe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:22:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add instructor 2FA (TOTP) and student email verification

Two of the auth-security recommendations from earlier in this thread,
implemented on top of the existing session/rate-limit/Brevo-email
infrastructure rather than adding new ones:

Instructors - mandatory TOTP 2FA (otplib), enrolled the first time an
instructor account (new or existing) completes a password check with no
totp_secret set yet. A server-side mfa_challenges row (10 min expiry)
carries the setup-in-progress secret across the extra round trip to
POST /api/auth/mfa/verify, so nothing is written onto the user row until
they've proven they can already generate a matching code with it. 8
bcrypt-hashed one-time backup codes are generated at enrolment and shown
once. QR code is rendered server-side (qrcode package) as a data URL, so
no third-party script needs loading client-side. Scoped to instructors
only, as asked - students and admins are unaffected.

Students - email verification gates login (not registration): register()
now sends a verification link instead of issuing a session for a new
student account; login blocks an unverified student with a clear message
and a resend option. Reuses the existing sendBrevoEmail/Brevo integration
(same one announcement emails already go through) and the email_verified
column that was already on the users table but never wired up to
anything. Token is a random 256-bit value, only its sha256 is stored,
24h expiry.

Frontend: login.html and signup.html's inline <script> blocks are now
external files (login.js/signup.js) - this was also the simplest way to
extend them without having to recompute and update their sha256 hashes
in the CSP header (script-src allows 'self', so external files need no
hash). New shared mfa.js renders the QR/code-entry/backup-codes overlay
used by both pages. New verify-email.html+js is the landing page for the
mailed link. auth.js's login()/register() no longer assume a response
always carries a user - pendingVerification/mfaRequired/mfaSetupRequired
responses carry none yet.

Known follow-up, not addressed here: the native Android app's
AuthRepository.login expects {user} straight back from /api/auth/login.
Since this is the same shared endpoint, an instructor logging in through
the native app will now get an mfaRequired/mfaSetupRequired response it
doesn't yet handle. Instructor-facing screens were already out of scope
for the native v1 build, but login itself wasn't - this needs a small
native MFA entry screen as a follow-up.

